# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Docker Compose overrides. Compose auto-loads this file when copied to
# `.env` (which is git-ignored):   cp .env.example .env
#
# Outbound proxy (NRI / Netskope corporate proxy — nriswg.nri.co.jp aka
# 163.116.128.80:8080).
#
# These are AICA_-namespaced ON PURPOSE. The WSL host shell already exports
# HTTP_PROXY/http_proxy for the corporate proxy; if compose read those directly
# it would leak a VPN-only proxy into the containers and break everything
# off-VPN. AICA_* is never set by the corporate environment, so:
#
#   • OFF the VPN / direct internet  → leave these BLANK (the default). The api
#     and ollama containers connect directly. Nothing to do.
#   • ON the corporate VPN           → uncomment the lines below so the api
#     container (Google Maps) and the ollama model pull route through the proxy.
#
# NOTE: this only sets the proxy INSIDE the containers. Docker *image pulls* use
# the daemon's own proxy (in /etc/docker/daemon.json on WSL), not this.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# AICA_HTTP_PROXY=http://nriswg.nri.co.jp:8080
# AICA_HTTPS_PROXY=http://nriswg.nri.co.jp:8080
# AICA_NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,api,ollama
